{
  "sticker": "pinecone",
  "skeleton": "pinecone with no limbs: root at its foot; body (the whole cone) with squash; face on the body with eyes and mouth; an open-scales piece swaps in for the body when it opens.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a pinecone character. Draw this exact pinecone as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the pinecone: the whole pinecone with its scales closed, as in image 1, with a completely blank face — the face area smooth with no eyes and no mouth — keep the rosy cheeks.\n2. the open pinecone: the same pinecone with its scales spread wide open like a flower, its face area just as blank.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a pinecone character; image 2 shows the same pinecone cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the pinecone's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the pinecone in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the pinecone's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile.\n7. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n8. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n9. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
